      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105416",
      ":question/problem": "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,g(t)={sin}^{2}\u2061t-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)\u22a5{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}$ equals $-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.$"
    },
