      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105411",
      ":question/problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,q(t)=7t-3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)\u22a5{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $2{t}^{2}+2t.$"
